# /etc/fw_env.config — U-Boot environment location on Advantech ECU-1170-552A eMMC
# Format: device  offset  size  [sectorsize  [nrofcopies]]
# Source: https://github.com/sbabic/libubootenv
#
# ECU-1170-552A eMMC layout assumption:
#   /dev/mmcblk0 = 64GB eMMC (boot + A/B rootfs + data)
#   U-Boot environment at 0x3E0000 offset on raw eMMC device
#   Environment block size: 0x20000 (128KB)
#   eMMC sector size: 0x200 (512 bytes)
#
# NOTE: This offset (0x3E0000) is the TI AM65xx-evm typical value.
# MUST be verified against CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET in the actual U-Boot defconfig
# used on the ECU-1170. If this offset is wrong, fw_printenv will report
# "Warning: Bad CRC, using default environment" and OTA A/B switching will fail.
# TODO (Phase 29): Confirm with Advantech BSP or read from U-Boot build config.
#
# To verify on target hardware:
#   fw_printenv -c /etc/fw_env.config ems_active_slot
# Expected output: "ems_active_slot=a" (or "b" for slot B)
# If output is empty or shows CRC warning, the offset is incorrect.
/dev/mmcblk0	0x3E0000	0x20000	0x200	1
/dev/mmcblk0	0x3E0000	0x20000	0x200	1
